WEBVTT

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:01.480
<i>Go forward...</i>

00:00:03.910 --> 00:00:04.950
<i>Forward!</i>

00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:08.430
<i>I won't run away...</i>

00:00:20.690 --> 00:00:21.620
<i>Not anymore!</i>

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:24.370
<i>I won't go back!</i>

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:30.930
<i>Go forward...</i>

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:42.020
<i>with all my power!</i>

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:53.610
I knew that you could do 
it if you tried, brother.

00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:59.620
I wish I could have seen you do more.

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:07.710
Til! Til! Til!

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:11.940
<i>I swear I won't run away anymore.</i>

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:13.080
<i>I won't go back.</i>

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:14.270
<i>I won't stop.</i>

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:17.030
<i>Even if my legs break, 
even if I can no longer see,</i>

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:19.010
<i>I'll keep running forward.</i>

00:01:19.630 --> 00:01:22.980
<i>And you'll be watching 
me from somewhere,</i>

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:24.020
<i>won't you, Til?</i>

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.980
<i>And so I started running to 
the center of the world.</i>

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:04.110
<i>The continent of Consume, 
a land where war never stops.</i>

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:08.080
<i>There, the blue-eyed Segua Kingdom</i>

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:10.570
<i>and the Red-Eyed Ninteldo Empire</i>

00:03:10.570 --> 00:03:14.190
<i>struggled for control of the land.</i>

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:15.750
<i>But for the last few years,</i>

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:17.750
<i>with the ascension of Emperor Marcus,</i>

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:20.290
<i>the forces of Ninteldo rapidly grew in power,</i>

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:25.030
<i>and they and their allies 
controlled 90% of the continent.</i>

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:29.020
<i>The Segua Kingdom was losing the war.</i>

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:34.980
The Hard Wars of Consume

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:38.650
Capital of Segua, Outori

00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:41.000
We finally made it, Til.

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:43.030
Vice-General Ramses!

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:44.960
You're being very loud.

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:46.310
What's wrong?

00:03:46.310 --> 00:03:48.890
M-My apologies, Vice-General Ramses.

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:50.870
A strange man is asking to 
be let into the military.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:52.650
Who?

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:56.130
He's definitely a Seguaian, 
but I don't know about him...

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:58.340
He says his name is Gear.

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:00.010
Gear?

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:06.670
So you're the one who wants 
to join our army, right?

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:09.770
Um, I want to join the Segua army.

00:04:10.130 --> 00:04:10.930
Please!

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:14.460
<i>I knew it. He's...</i>

00:04:16.270 --> 00:04:18.440
Very well, I understand.

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:20.660
Gear, correct?

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:23.450
If you want to join the army,

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:27.390
you must fight here and 
prove your strength.

00:04:27.390 --> 00:04:28.940
Fight everyone here.

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:31.660
B-But that's crazy!

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:33.550
Does that not satisfy you?

00:04:33.550 --> 00:04:35.280
No, I understand.

00:04:36.570 --> 00:04:39.810
There are 50 of the regular 
army's best men here.

00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:43.720
Now show me your Killer Power!

00:04:44.110 --> 00:04:44.720
Begin!

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:54.490
Wow!

00:04:54.490 --> 00:04:56.570
He moved so fast!

00:04:56.570 --> 00:04:57.480
Could you see that?

00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:58.940
What was that?

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:05.290
<i>I won't run away anymore. 
I'll go forward!</i>

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:11.120
<i>I'll prove my power!</i>

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:12.800
<i>He wiped them all out?</i>

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:14.300
<i>In just a few minutes?</i>

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:17.120
<i>He's far beyond what I imagined!</i>

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:19.420
Stop right there, kid.

00:05:20.410 --> 00:05:21.180
Not yet.

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:23.630
It's still too early to get cocky.

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:26.630
<i>The strongest man in the Segua army.</i>

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:28.960
<i>Harris, the Captain of Defenses.</i>

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:32.140
You're fast, I'll admit that.

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:35.810
But do you have power?

00:05:38.490 --> 00:05:39.590
What?

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:45.410
<i>There it is!</i>

00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:48.280
<i>He's what I've been waiting for!</i>

00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:53.290
<i>With him here, I can make it real.</i>

00:05:56.800 --> 00:05:58.760
<i>A new era for Segua!</i>

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:03.130
That was great, brother!

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:07.640
<i>I can take back our share 
of Consume from Ninteldo,</i>

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:09.640
<i>and end the Hard Wars!</i>

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:13.680
Ninteldo Territory

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:23.220
I told you!

00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:27.400
Games like you don't know a thing!

00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:32.410
Here in Consume...

00:06:35.890 --> 00:06:38.090
things won't work that way.

00:07:05.140 --> 00:07:06.320
It's over.

00:07:07.930 --> 00:07:09.760
People kept going on about how great

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:12.170
their specs were before 
they actually showed up,

00:07:12.170 --> 00:07:13.820
but they were crap.

00:07:15.470 --> 00:07:19.360
There's no one left on Consume 
who can stand against us.

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:22.160
I guess all that's left is Segua.

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:24.840
I heard rumors they're going 
to try something soon.

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:27.500
Segua?

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:31.040
It doesn't matter what Segua does.

00:07:31.040 --> 00:07:33.950
Ninteldo has but one goal.

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:36.100
And I believe that

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:41.350
heaven has entrusted us with it.

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:46.290
To be honest, things don't look good.

00:07:46.290 --> 00:07:50.670
Ninteldo and its allies control 
90% of the continent.

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:53.860
But the next operation is the 
beginning of our counterattack.

00:07:54.600 --> 00:07:56.590
Our target is Hope Fortress,

00:07:56.590 --> 00:07:59.620
in one of the countries allied 
to Ninteldo, "Tetrand."

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:03.060
We'll rescue General Alex, 
who's being held there.

00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:06.630
Gear, I'm putting you in charge

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:09.010
of the first special forces 
squad for the mission.

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:14.130
This is all moving a little too fast...

00:08:14.540 --> 00:08:17.270
It's the most important task 
in the upcoming operation.

00:08:17.270 --> 00:08:18.470
Is that not enough?

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:20.470
No, it's plenty.

00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:23.390
You can beat up those Ninteldo guys!

00:08:23.740 --> 00:08:25.610
You're great!

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:26.860
Go get 'em!

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:29.190
Let's all do our best 
in the next operation.

00:08:29.720 --> 00:08:33.850
I didn't know Segua still 
had warriors like you.

00:08:33.850 --> 00:08:35.290
Where have you been?

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:45.620
Opal!

00:08:47.310 --> 00:08:48.730
What are you—

00:08:48.730 --> 00:08:50.510
Just saying hello.

00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:58.580
I was watching from above.

00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:00.470
You're putting him in the 
special forces squad?

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:03.110
This is Opal,

00:09:03.110 --> 00:09:05.480
one of the special 
forces, just like you.

00:09:06.010 --> 00:09:08.720
She's the second strongest 
in the Segua army.

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:11.970
General Alex is the strongest,

00:09:11.970 --> 00:09:13.890
but he's been captured by the enemy.

00:09:13.890 --> 00:09:17.490
So right now, she's the strongest 
we have in our army.

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:19.310
I'm Gear.

00:09:19.310 --> 00:09:20.300
Nice to meet you.

00:09:20.300 --> 00:09:22.480
I-I'm Nel!

00:09:23.730 --> 00:09:26.500
W-Well, for today you should rest.

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:29.040
I'll have a room prepared.

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:30.310
We can go over the details tomorrow.

00:09:33.480 --> 00:09:34.880
It's so soft!

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:37.510
I haven't slept in a 
bed like this in ages.

00:09:40.660 --> 00:09:41.670
A letter?

00:09:41.670 --> 00:09:43.350
Yeah, looks like it.

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:47.870
I'm tired.

00:09:47.870 --> 00:09:49.120
Let's get to sleep.

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:49.840
Yeah.

00:09:58.310 --> 00:09:59.530
What do you want?

00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:02.120
Calling me out at this hour.

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:05.120
I'm amazed you didn't run away.

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:09.120
I'll be up front with you: 
I don't like you!

00:10:09.320 --> 00:10:10.140
What?

00:10:10.600 --> 00:10:13.520
I don't want to fight in the 
special forces with you.

00:10:13.990 --> 00:10:15.570
Fight me!

00:10:15.570 --> 00:10:19.130
If you win, I'll do whatever you want.

00:10:19.130 --> 00:10:20.220
But if I win...

00:10:21.730 --> 00:10:23.720
You leave the castle!

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:28.730
All right, if that's what 
it takes to satisfy you.

00:10:30.030 --> 00:10:32.270
That's the attitude I hate!

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:35.400
You think if you show how strong you are, 
everything will go your way.

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:37.990
You get off on beating 
people weaker than you.

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:39.940
Just like him...

00:10:40.790 --> 00:10:43.490
I hate men like you 
more than anything!

00:10:43.790 --> 00:10:45.990
I saw your power back there.

00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:48.750
It's not fair unless I show you mine.

00:10:49.010 --> 00:10:51.900
Throw that rock there at me.

00:10:53.110 --> 00:10:54.180
Like this?

00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:01.010
Got it?

00:11:01.010 --> 00:11:03.480
No matter how fast you are,

00:11:03.480 --> 00:11:05.600
I'll never miss.

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:08.890
I'm not stupid enough to 
kill another Seguaian.

00:11:08.890 --> 00:11:11.990
Whoever lands the first 
solid hit wins.

00:11:11.990 --> 00:11:12.880
Got it?

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:13.810
Yeah.

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:17.520
Then let's get started.

00:11:17.520 --> 00:11:20.360
When this pebble hits 
the ground, we begin.

00:11:20.360 --> 00:11:21.590
Okay.

00:11:23.420 --> 00:11:24.400
<i>I've won.</i>

00:11:24.400 --> 00:11:26.830
<i>My victory is already assured!</i>

00:11:26.830 --> 00:11:30.000
<i>He's probably going to go 
around to dodge the arrow,</i>

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:33.280
<i>but he has to get close to attack.</i>

00:11:33.800 --> 00:11:35.900
<i>He'll leap towards me.</i>

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:38.630
<i>And when he does, he's mine!</i>

00:11:40.190 --> 00:11:41.720
<i>You're just a barbarian.</i>

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:43.390
<i>You can't beat me.</i>

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:47.310
Unlike you, I've fought 
for years and years.

00:11:47.310 --> 00:11:50.390
You're just an arrogant rat who's 
come down from the mountains!

00:11:51.950 --> 00:11:53.000
And that arrogance ends here!

00:11:55.090 --> 00:11:56.480
<i>He's coming straight 
at me, and he's fast!</i>

00:12:09.760 --> 00:12:10.560
Huh?

00:12:11.060 --> 00:12:12.160
Oh, you're awake?

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:13.660
What are you doing?

00:12:13.660 --> 00:12:15.000
Put me down!

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:16.580
You were out cold.

00:12:16.230 --> 00:12:17.370
Let me go!

00:12:16.580 --> 00:12:19.170
I couldn't leave you out 
on the beach at night.

00:12:20.860 --> 00:12:23.490
Maybe everybody thinks 
I'm full of myself

00:12:23.490 --> 00:12:25.180
because I beat them,

00:12:25.180 --> 00:12:26.790
but that's not true.

00:12:26.790 --> 00:12:29.890
I just wanted everyone to accept me,

00:12:29.890 --> 00:12:32.170
and to help Segua as fast as I could.

00:12:32.780 --> 00:12:35.190
You're right. I've been hiding in the 
mountains until a short time ago.

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:38.150
I wasn't trying to go forward.

00:12:38.760 --> 00:12:41.350
I didn't realize how stupid I was.

00:12:43.350 --> 00:12:45.530
Until my best friend died...

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:49.370
You guys have been fighting 
for years, right?

00:12:49.780 --> 00:12:52.020
So I respect all of you...

00:12:53.480 --> 00:12:57.180
All of you that had already 
been moving forward

00:12:57.180 --> 00:12:58.420
years before me.

00:12:59.810 --> 00:13:02.500
<i>I guess he's not so bad.</i>

00:13:02.500 --> 00:13:04.730
<i>He's just really straightforward.</i>

00:13:05.430 --> 00:13:07.590
<i>I'll have to apologize later.</i>

00:13:17.910 --> 00:13:19.230
That's far enough.

00:13:20.200 --> 00:13:22.020
I can walk the rest of the way.

00:13:23.660 --> 00:13:26.350
So, what should I do?

00:13:26.350 --> 00:13:26.950
Huh?

00:13:26.950 --> 00:13:29.330
Well... you know...

00:13:29.970 --> 00:13:34.300
I said that if you won, I'd do anything...

00:13:35.730 --> 00:13:36.960
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:40.940
<i>I was so sure I wouldn't lose, 
I got carried away!</i>

00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:50.220
But that wasn't really my victory.

00:13:50.790 --> 00:13:53.570
You hesitated because that arrow

00:13:53.570 --> 00:13:56.480
would've hit me right 
in the head, didn't you?

00:13:56.960 --> 00:13:58.980
I thought to myself that 
you were a lot nicer

00:13:58.980 --> 00:14:00.240
than you looked.

00:14:01.690 --> 00:14:02.730
A loss is a loss!

00:14:03.150 --> 00:14:05.280
Give me your order already!

00:14:07.510 --> 00:14:09.300
Okay, got it.

00:14:09.300 --> 00:14:10.290
Then...

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:14.860
Let's fight together from now on, okay?

00:14:21.430 --> 00:14:22.820
Okay...

00:14:28.140 --> 00:14:31.640
Ramses-san, when does the 
special forces mission start?

00:14:31.950 --> 00:14:34.460
The two of us will execute it perfectly!

00:14:36.110 --> 00:14:37.530
We can do this!

00:14:37.530 --> 00:14:40.200
If Gear and I work together,

00:14:40.200 --> 00:14:41.400
and the gears mesh...

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:44.390
Was that not hilarious?

00:14:44.390 --> 00:14:45.450
No, it wasn't.

00:14:45.450 --> 00:14:48.370
I'm glad the two of 
you are friends now.

00:14:48.370 --> 00:14:51.720
<i>Why are the two of them 
friends all of a sudden?</i>

00:14:52.360 --> 00:14:55.340
I called you here to introduce

00:14:55.340 --> 00:14:57.740
the other member of the special forces.

00:14:58.490 --> 00:15:00.110
Other member?

00:15:00.110 --> 00:15:01.580
Is it somebody I know?

00:15:01.830 --> 00:15:04.830
No, he's not a Seguaian.

00:15:04.830 --> 00:15:07.040
So he's a mercenary?

00:15:07.040 --> 00:15:08.780
You paid money to hire him?

00:15:08.780 --> 00:15:09.590
That's right.

00:15:10.210 --> 00:15:12.920
Will that really be okay?

00:15:12.920 --> 00:15:14.890
Yes. I'm confident in his skills.

00:15:15.360 --> 00:15:18.080
There aren't any warriors 
who are a match

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:19.850
for you two in Segua.

00:15:20.360 --> 00:15:21.810
His name is Tejirof.

00:15:22.410 --> 00:15:26.980
He was my upperclassman 
at Puzzle Magic Academy.

00:15:28.920 --> 00:15:30.490
What's he like?

00:15:30.490 --> 00:15:31.970
Hmm...

00:15:31.970 --> 00:15:33.810
I guess the best word 
would be "genius."

00:15:33.810 --> 00:15:36.990
A genius at theory.

00:15:37.470 --> 00:15:40.730
A genius at theory?

00:15:42.210 --> 00:15:44.060
He'll be here soon.

00:15:44.060 --> 00:15:46.340
He's supposed to arrive 
in about five minutes.

00:15:46.340 --> 00:15:47.730
He sounds like the kind of guy

00:15:47.730 --> 00:15:49.970
who'd show up right on time.

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:50.990
Yeah.

00:15:50.990 --> 00:15:52.260
I can't wait to meet him.

00:16:00.350 --> 00:16:03.900
One hour later...

00:16:03.160 --> 00:16:04.270
Isn't he late?

00:16:04.850 --> 00:16:06.270
This is strange.

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:09.210
<i>This isn't exactly the best start.</i>

00:16:10.140 --> 00:16:10.940
He's here.

00:16:12.060 --> 00:16:13.700
Oh, hey there.

00:16:14.230 --> 00:16:18.450
I was busy pleasuring 
myself and so I'm late.

00:16:20.100 --> 00:16:22.330
Ramses, it's been a while.

00:16:31.210 --> 00:16:33.790
You're as hot as ever.

00:16:33.790 --> 00:16:35.390
Let me stick it in later.

00:16:35.390 --> 00:16:37.970
Just go sit down.

00:16:38.950 --> 00:16:41.980
I heard things are bad because 
your general was captured.

00:16:42.780 --> 00:16:44.480
Well, don't worry.

00:16:44.840 --> 00:16:49.980
I'll plug my stick in the 
hole left by your general.

00:16:53.070 --> 00:16:55.410
<i>Is this really going to work?</i>

00:16:59.530 --> 00:17:00.490
I see.

00:17:01.010 --> 00:17:03.270
I more or less understand 
the situation.

00:17:03.270 --> 00:17:05.750
It's going to be hard 
with just these two.

00:17:06.380 --> 00:17:09.600
The girl with the big 
rack and the new kid.

00:17:09.600 --> 00:17:11.680
My breasts don't have 
anything to do with it!

00:17:11.680 --> 00:17:13.010
What about the girl with the ears?

00:17:13.810 --> 00:17:17.760
No, I can't fight...

00:17:19.570 --> 00:17:20.810
Well, that's fine.

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:23.520
How much time do we have 
left until the operation?

00:17:23.830 --> 00:17:25.110
Four days.

00:17:25.110 --> 00:17:26.360
Four days, huh?

00:17:26.360 --> 00:17:28.310
That's plenty.

00:17:28.310 --> 00:17:29.890
Okay, got it.

00:17:29.890 --> 00:17:32.130
I'll train you hard for the four days

00:17:32.130 --> 00:17:34.030
until the operation starts.

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:38.520
Your defenses are full of holes.

00:17:38.520 --> 00:17:41.290
I'll poke my stick in all over.

00:17:46.200 --> 00:17:47.120
Okay.

00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:48.540
Then let's get started.

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:51.550
<i>Is this really okay?</i>

00:17:51.820 --> 00:17:54.050
Let's start with you, new kid.

00:17:54.810 --> 00:17:57.050
You think I'm weak, don't you?

00:17:57.860 --> 00:17:58.550
That's fine.

00:17:58.970 --> 00:18:00.800
First come at me as hard as you can.

00:18:01.480 --> 00:18:03.970
And I'll carve this into your memory:

00:18:03.970 --> 00:18:06.490
"The first person I met 
who was stronger than me

00:18:06.490 --> 00:18:09.560
was a pervert with a 
thing for dirty jokes."

00:18:09.560 --> 00:18:10.560
Ready?

00:18:12.290 --> 00:18:15.350
Let's see the power that got you into

00:18:15.350 --> 00:18:18.320
the special forces squad 
on your first day!

00:18:20.940 --> 00:18:21.700
He's fast!

00:18:23.870 --> 00:18:24.700
But...

00:18:27.590 --> 00:18:30.240
This stops him.

00:18:35.710 --> 00:18:36.320
Brother!

00:18:36.320 --> 00:18:38.290
He was able to see through Gear's speed?

00:18:40.160 --> 00:18:42.990
You weren't running with 
your best technique.

00:18:42.990 --> 00:18:47.040
Maybe it feels good to run as 
fast as you can like that,

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:51.110
but that only works on the first stage.

00:18:51.460 --> 00:18:54.550
If you want to survive, 
cast aside those feelings.

00:18:54.930 --> 00:18:56.110
Do you understand?

00:18:56.750 --> 00:19:00.110
Fighting on a battlefield 
means killing.

00:19:00.110 --> 00:19:02.620
You can't fight a real battle 
based off how you feel.

00:19:04.350 --> 00:19:05.370
<i>I lost.</i>

00:19:05.920 --> 00:19:07.310
<i>I completely lost.</i>

00:19:10.260 --> 00:19:11.280
<i>Til.</i>

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:16.130
<i>Am I really unworthy of your respect?</i>

00:19:16.770 --> 00:19:19.510
<i>No, I made a promise!</i>

00:19:20.170 --> 00:19:23.270
<i>Nobody starts at the goal.</i>

00:19:23.270 --> 00:19:26.450
<i>I swore to run to the goal!</i>

00:19:29.880 --> 00:19:33.190
<i>No matter how many times 
I go down on the way!</i>

00:19:38.840 --> 00:19:40.480
Are you okay, brother?

00:19:40.480 --> 00:19:41.480
Brother?

00:19:42.610 --> 00:19:43.780
Morning.

00:19:44.430 --> 00:19:47.610
How did you enjoy your first beating?

00:19:49.030 --> 00:19:51.040
Sure, you're strong.

00:19:51.530 --> 00:19:55.040
But there are a lot of people on 
the battlefield who are stronger.

00:19:55.520 --> 00:19:58.620
I'd imagine you'll meet a few 
of them during the operation.

00:19:59.420 --> 00:20:02.500
Are you prepared to go anyway, new kid?

00:20:03.090 --> 00:20:05.990
Or will you give up and 
go back to training?

00:20:05.990 --> 00:20:06.810
No,

00:20:07.440 --> 00:20:08.760
I won't stop.

00:20:09.240 --> 00:20:10.260
I'm going.

00:20:10.830 --> 00:20:13.410
I decided I'd go straight ahead!

00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:15.980
No hesitation.

00:20:16.610 --> 00:20:17.570
I see.

00:20:17.910 --> 00:20:20.000
For your dead friend?

00:20:20.630 --> 00:20:21.820
How did you know?

00:20:22.860 --> 00:20:23.810
Was I right?

00:20:24.390 --> 00:20:26.830
Well, it was the only 
logical deduction.

00:20:27.500 --> 00:20:29.300
I figured something like that was

00:20:29.300 --> 00:20:32.160
the only way to get a 
coward to come down from

00:20:32.160 --> 00:20:34.080
the mountain he was hiding on.

00:20:34.450 --> 00:20:36.240
You're trying to go straight forward,

00:20:36.240 --> 00:20:38.350
to make up for all the time 
you spent at a standstill?

00:20:38.350 --> 00:20:39.510
Pretty simple.

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:41.590
No matter what you say,

00:20:41.590 --> 00:20:44.010
I'm going to follow my own path!

00:20:44.520 --> 00:20:47.210
No, I'm not saying it's a bad thing.

00:20:47.210 --> 00:20:48.390
I think it's fine.

00:20:48.880 --> 00:20:51.890
I think there's nothing 
wrong with your answer.

00:20:52.600 --> 00:20:54.800
I don't like people who aren't 
straight with others.

00:20:55.200 --> 00:20:57.400
You should go as deep 
as you can with it.

00:20:58.090 --> 00:20:59.480
A stick...

00:21:00.330 --> 00:21:03.900
doesn't feel good unless 
you stick it straight in.

00:21:04.300 --> 00:21:05.570
Go straight ahead.

00:21:06.170 --> 00:21:09.020
I hope you find your real answer there.

00:21:13.300 --> 00:21:15.340
Tejirof, I'm sorry!

00:21:15.840 --> 00:21:18.420
I had the wrong idea about you.

00:21:18.790 --> 00:21:20.610
I want to be stronger.

00:21:21.260 --> 00:21:23.670
So help me train!

00:21:24.340 --> 00:21:25.470
Sure.

00:21:25.470 --> 00:21:27.940
But rest a bit more today.

00:21:27.940 --> 00:21:30.180
You can read these 
while you're resting.

00:21:31.840 --> 00:21:32.930
What's this?

00:21:33.340 --> 00:21:36.940
The map of Hope Fortress, 
where we're headed.

00:21:37.330 --> 00:21:41.190
It was close to the port, 
so I took a look before I came here.

00:21:41.550 --> 00:21:45.170
I got a little too into it and so 
I was an hour late in arriving,

00:21:45.170 --> 00:21:48.450
but well, nobody told 
me to look for it.

00:21:48.740 --> 00:21:51.950
So this was me pleasuring myself.

00:21:53.390 --> 00:21:54.460
Bye.

00:21:58.250 --> 00:22:00.960
Nel, the world's a big place.

00:22:01.510 --> 00:22:04.100
<i>Til, I'm going to keep running!</i>

00:23:26.290 --> 00:23:28.740
That was the incident known 
as the Atarika Shock.

00:23:28.740 --> 00:23:29.840
"Shooting."

00:23:29.840 --> 00:23:31.800
No, I can't hold it in anymore!

00:23:31.800 --> 00:23:33.550
You seem to have a knack for Online.

00:23:33.550 --> 00:23:35.140
Like how that girl's nice...

00:23:35.140 --> 00:23:36.820
I want to be strong anyway!

00:23:36.810 --> 00:23:39.890
Episode 2 is Being Worked On Right Now!

00:23:36.820 --> 00:23:39.940
Is that why this operation is so cruel?
